  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening risk-based food control in Sub-Saharan Africa: implementation of a regional Total Diet Study as a tool to assess food chemical contamination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Main: To strengthen the risk-based food control in Sub-Saharan Africa by the mean of the Total Diet Study (TDS) as a tool to assess food chemical concentration. br  Specific: br  (i) To provide risk managers with the scientific basis needed to carry out its activities to protect human health br  (ii) To promote safe food production and trade at both national and international level.</narrative>
  </description>
